# Lossy encode per-phase wall-clock baseline at e2..=e5 (W38, 2026-05-19)

## Provenance

- Date: 2026-05-18 UTC (post-W36-1 extension downward in effort space)
- Hostname: lilith (water-cooled AMD Ryzen 9 7950X, 32 threads, 128 GB RAM)
- Parent commit: 70a48af9 (W36-1 baseline at e6/e7/e8)
- Workspace: ~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--low-effort-baseline (jj sibling on main)
- Encoder build: release, features `std parallel butteraugli-loop`
- Sweep wall: 42.1s (JXL phase sweep only; cross-codec table in companion file)

## Tool choice

Identical pattern to W36-1: subprocess-per-encode driven by `examples/lossy_low_effort_zenjpeg_compare.rs`. Each subprocess sets `__JXL_ENC_PHASE_TIMING=1` so the existing `eprintln!` markers in `vardct::encoder::encode_inner` and `vardct::bitstream::encode_two_pass_to_writer` emit a single summary line per encode; the parent captures stderr and parses the `key=value` pairs. Default encodes (env var unset) are byte-identical to main (hash_lock contract preserved).

## Sweep grid

- 8 images: same as W36-1 (5 CID22-512 photos: 1025469/1044329/1189261/1279330/1418519 + 3 GB82-SC screenshots: codec_wiki/imac_g3/terminal). Photos 512×512 (0.26 MP). Screenshots 2560×1664 / 2940×1912 / 1646×1062.
- 4 distances: 0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0
- 4 efforts: 2, 3, 4, 5 (extends W36-1's 6/7/8 downward)
- 3 runs per cell (384 encodes total); median per phase kept

## Reproducer

```bash
cargo build -p jxl-encoder --release --features 'std parallel butteraugli-loop' \
    --example lossy_low_effort_zenjpeg_compare
./target/release/examples/lossy_low_effort_zenjpeg_compare \
    --out-jxl benchmarks/lossy_phase_baseline_low_effort_2026-05-19.tsv \
    --out-cross benchmarks/lossy_phase_low_effort_with_zenjpeg_2026-05-19.tsv
```

